---
title: "Checkout — reservation protocol (ADR-0003, supersedes specification §3.4)"
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Client
    participant S as SPA
    participant O as order-service
    participant K as Keycloak
    participant CAT as catalog-service
    participant DBO as db_order
    participant DBC as db_catalog

    C->>S: "Confirm order"
    S->>O: POST /api/v1/orders<br/>Bearer <user token>
    O->>O: customerId = jwt.sub<br/>(never from the request body)

    rect rgb(238, 246, 255)
        Note over O,DBC: PHASE 1 — reserve.<br/>One call returns availability AND the authoritative prices,<br/>so the price persisted below is the one that was validated.
        O->>K: client_credentials grant
        K-->>O: machine token (role SERVICE)
        O->>CAT: POST /internal/v1/stock/reservations<br/>{ orderRef, lines[] }
        CAT->>DBC: BEGIN
        CAT->>DBC: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE on the products
        CAT->>DBC: available = stock_quantity − active reservations
        alt any line short
            CAT->>DBC: ROLLBACK — all-or-nothing, nothing is held
            CAT-->>O: 409 problem+json<br/>{ type: insufficient-stock, shortages[] }
            O-->>S: 409 naming the product that ran out
            S-->>C: "Insufficient stock: MOD-SPD-T2 (3 remaining)"
        else all lines available
            CAT->>DBC: INSERT reservation + lines<br/>expires_at = now + 15 min
            CAT->>DBC: COMMIT
            CAT-->>O: 201 { reservationId, expiresAt,<br/>lines[{ reference, label, unitPriceExclVat }] }
        end
    end

    rect rgb(240, 253, 244)
        Note over O,DBO: PHASE 2 — persist locally.<br/>If this fails, do NOTHING. No compensating call: a compensation<br/>issued by a process that may have just died is not a recovery<br/>mechanism. The reservation expires on its own.
        O->>DBO: BEGIN
        O->>DBO: INSERT orders (status = CREATED,<br/>reservation_id, total_excl_vat,<br/>vat_amount, total_incl_vat)
        O->>DBO: INSERT lines — price COPIED, not referenced (§3.3)
        O->>DBO: COMMIT
    end

    rect rgb(255, 247, 237)
        Note over O,DBC: PHASE 3 — confirm. Idempotent:<br/>the reservation row is a single-use token.
        O->>CAT: POST /internal/v1/stock/reservations/{id}/confirm
        CAT->>DBC: BEGIN
        CAT->>DBC: stock_quantity -= quantity
        CAT->>DBC: reservation.status = CONFIRMED
        CAT->>DBC: COMMIT
        CAT-->>O: 200
        O->>DBO: orders.status = CONFIRMED
    end

    O-->>S: 201 Created + Location: /api/v1/orders/{id}
    S-->>C: Order confirmation

    rect rgb(254, 242, 242)
        Note over CAT,DBC: RECOVERY — the property that makes this correct.<br/>Every repair runs inside catalog, as a local transaction, on the<br/>database that owns the stock. Nothing has to survive a crash.
        loop @Scheduled every 60 s
            CAT->>DBC: UPDATE reservation SET status = 'EXPIRED'<br/>WHERE status = 'ACTIVE' AND expires_at < now()
        end
        Note over O: An order stuck at CREATED whose reservation expired<br/>is reconciled to CANCELLED. No stock was ever lost.
    end
